          "message": "feat(reason-dl): DL L2 singleton owl:intersectionOf normalization + explicit-negative profile lane (sq-pbz04.4.16) [FABLE-5] (#1821)\n\n🤖 SPARQ agent. Two L2 follow-ups from the sq-pbz04.4.5 conformance arm, behind\nthe opt-in `dl-direct` feature (OFF by default; forwards to\n`sparq-reason-dl/dispatch`).\n\n(1) M7 — singleton owl:intersectionOf normalization. The OWL-1-era RDF encoding\n`_:B owl:intersectionOf ( :A )` (a one-member operand list) denotes `⊓{A}`,\nwhose Direct-Semantics interpretation is exactly its sole member `A` (Structural\nSpec §8.1). The official test-suite tagging normalizes this before profile\nchecking, but L2's structural-spec arity rule (≥ 2 members) rejected it as\n`NotIn`. `extract()` now performs the same model-preserving normalization at L1\n(a 1-ary intersection collapses to its member; ≥ 2-member intersections are\nUNCHANGED, so the arity rule stays intact for genuine intersections). All 27\npinned M7 positive-profile divergences (`WebOnt-I5.26-002`/`-005`,\n`WebOnt-disjointWith-003`…`-009`, each EL/QL/RL) now PASS — `PROFILE_DIVERGENCES`\nis empty and `DL_PROFILE_FLOOR` rises 68 → 95.\n\nReasoning-lane consequence (honest, verified): 8 consistency cases\n(`WebOnt-disjointWith-003`…`-009`, `WebOnt-I5.26-005`) that were out-of-profile\nby their arity-1 shape (routed to the ALCH tableau → definitive `Consistent`)\nare now correctly IN-RL, so dispatch routes them to the RL branch, which\nfail-closed ABSTAINS via the documented `RlDivergenceGuard(\"owl:disjointWith\")`\n(RL rule-set incompleteness on disjointness). Never a wrong verdict — the fail\nset is UNCHANGED at 5 (M3/M5/M6). `DL_DIRECT_FLOOR` re-pinned 190 → 182,\n`DL_DIRECT_ABSTAINED` 464 → 472, deliberately with the mechanism documented.\n\n(2) Explicit-negative profile lane. The export's manifest-level\n`owl:NegativePropertyAssertion(case, test:profile, {EL|QL|RL})` triples are now\nwired as explicit-negation expectations (driven `expect_in = false`) into a\nSEPARATE `DlReport::profile_negative` lane. HONEST measured In-vs-negative gap:\n180 of 319 checkable (refuted 139), improved from the pre-lane measurement\n211/322. An `In` verdict on a negation is the honest L2 limitation (axiom-grammar\nmembership over the ALCH shadow cannot refute FULL-profile membership — anonymous\nindividuals, datatype maps, global/species constraints unimplemented, design\nrecord §4/§5 deferred), pinned as a FALL-only gap floor, never asserted to zero,\nkept OUT of the positive lane's fail set so the positive floor never moves.\n\nGates GREEN in BOTH feature states (default OFF + `dl-direct` ON): clippy\n--all-targets -D warnings, sparq-reason-dl tests, dl_suite ratchet (2 passed),\nscoreboard_floors textual guard (4 passed), rustdoc --workspace --no-deps\n--all-features -D warnings. New direct unit tests: normalize_intersection,\nextract_singleton_intersection_normalizes_to_member, collect_profile_negations.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <jesse@jeswr.org>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-10T03:55:45Z",
